codex
The APIs and multi-call equivalence tests are in place. Processing uses shared handles where C only reads the schedule, and exclusive handles for AES/CTR state. I also found that random-IV generation can reach an unsynchronized C fallback, so it now shares a lock with the existing seed wrapper. Validation is underway across sanitizers, Miri, compile-fail doctests, and coverage.
